<title>UK: Bernard Matthews H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Bernard Matthews H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending July 14</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		5.76		   vs 4.74</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.70		   vs 1.39</p>
<p> Pretax		     10.43		  vs 8.67</p>
<p> Turnover		   172.36		 vs 144.90</p>
<p>NOTE - Poultry meat specialist producer Bernard Matthews Plc said almost all the increase in turnover and profits came from extra sales of branded added value products in frozen, fresh and cooked meat sectors.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement that although results had benefited from higher demand for poultry meat following fears over bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE), &quot;sales were already running at significantly higher levels before the BSE crisis occurred.&quot;</p>
</text>
